# Cline / Roo Code / VS Code Rules: Multi-Agent System Bridge (.agents)

You are operating within a codebase governed by a Multi-Agent Architecture located in `.agents/`.

## 1. System Protocols
- Always follow `.agents/AGENTS.md` for role expectations, handoffs, and task dispatching.
- Comply with all `.agents/rules/*.md`:
  - `00-git-workflow.md`: Always work on dedicated branches (`feature/*`, `fix/*`), never direct to `main`/`master`.
  - `01-codebase-scouting.md`: Progressive file discovery, avoid reading entire codebases in bulk.
  - `02-agent-handoff-protocol.md`: Use Task Dispatch Contracts and structured Handoff Reports.
  - `03-frontend-standards.md`: Rich aesthetics, modern design tokens, accessible DOM.
  - `04-backend-standards.md`: Clean route contracts, schema validations, robust database migrations.
  - `05-fullstack-integration.md`: Complete vertical slice development, end-to-end type safety.
  - `06-bug-triage-and-patching.md`: 4-step forensic triage: root cause -> repro test -> patch -> verification.
  - `07-quality-and-security.md`: OWASP Top 10 checklist, deterministic tests.

## 2. Skill Execution
- Consult `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` for specific step-by-step procedures when acting as a specialized engineer.
